# GPS Tracker — Android conventions

## Architecture

- Single `app` module, package-by-feature under `com.example.gpstracker`.
- Layers: `core/{designsystem,navigation,common,data,location,permissions}` and `feature/*`.
- MVVM + UDF: ViewModel exposes `StateFlow<UiState>`; UI sends events up. No business logic in Composables.
- One-shot navigation/snackbars via `EventBus` + `ObserveAsEvents` — never put `NavController` in a ViewModel.
- Inject `DispatcherProvider`; do IO with `withContext(io)` / `flowOn(io)`, CPU work with `default`. Keep the UI thread free.
- Add `domain/` only when real logic needs it. Feature `data/` only when that feature owns persistence/network.

## UI

- Jetpack Compose + Material 3 only (no XML layouts for screens).
- Use `AppTheme` and design-system components (`AppButton`, `AppCard`, `ToolTile`, `StatusChip`, `ProBadge`, `AppTopBar`).
- No hardcoded user-facing strings → `strings.xml`.
- No hardcoded colors or spacing → theme / `LocalSpacing` tokens.
- Icons require content descriptions; interactive targets ≥ 48dp.

## Navigation

- Type-safe `@Serializable` routes in `core/navigation/Route.kt`.
- Bottom bar only on Home / Saved / History / Settings.
- Start destination decided by DataStore `onboardingCompleted`.

## Dependencies & secrets

- Do not add libraries outside the approved version catalog without asking.
- API keys via Secrets Gradle Plugin: `local.properties` + `secrets.defaults.properties`. Never commit real keys.

## Permissions

- Manifest may only include `INTERNET` and `ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE` unless the user explicitly approves more.
- Camera / GPS / compass stay `uses-feature required="false"`.

## Testing

- Prefer ViewModel unit tests with JUnit (+ coroutines-test when async).
- Keep `./gradlew assembleDebug` and `./gradlew testDebugUnitTest` green.
